The equation of a plane can be written in the form $Ax + By + Cz + D = 0.$  Two planes with normal vectors $\mathbf{n}_1$ and $\mathbf{n}_2$ are perpendicular if and only if $\mathbf{n}_1 \cdot \mathbf{n}_2 = 0.$

[asy]
import three;

size(180);
currentprojection = perspective(6,3,2);

triple I = (1,0,0), J = (0,1,0), K = (0,0,1), O = (0,-0.5,0);
triple A = (1,0,0), B = (0,1,0), C = (0,0,1), P = (-5,-1,-5);

draw(surface((2*I + 2*J)--(2*I - 2*J)--(-2*I - 2*J)--(-2*I + 2*J)--cycle),paleyellow,nolight);
draw((2*I + 2*J)--(2*I - 2*J)--(-2*I - 2*J)--(-2*I + 2*J)--cycle);
draw(surface((2*I + 2*K)--(2*I - 2*K)--(-2*I - 2*K)--(-2*I + 2*K)--cycle),paleyellow,nolight);
draw((2*I + 2*K)--(2*I - 2*K)--(-2*I - 2*K)--(-2*I + 2*K)--cycle);
draw(surface((2*J + 2*K)--(2*J - 2*K)--(-2*J - 2*K)--(-2*J + 2*K)--cycle),paleyellow,nolight);
draw((2*J + 2*K)--(2*J - 2*K)--(-2*J - 2*K)--(-2*J + 2*K)--cycle);
draw((0,0,0)--P,Arrow3(6));
draw(O--1.5*(3*I - 6*J + 2*K),Arrow3(6));
draw(O--1.5*(4*I - 12*J + 3*K),Arrow3(6));

label("$x$", 2.2*I);
label("$y$", 2.2*J);
label("$z$", 2.2*K);
label("$\mathbf{n}_1$", (3*I - 6*J + 2*K), N);
label("$\mathbf{n}_2$", (4*I - 12*J + 3*K), NE);
label("$(-5,-1,-5)$", P, S);
[/asy]

The normal vector of the plane $3x - 6y + 2z + 5 = 0$ is $\mathbf{n}_1 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -6 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix},$ and the normal vector of the plane $4x - 12y + 3z - 3 = 0$ is $\mathbf{n}_2 = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -12 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}.$

Let $\mathbf{n}$ be the normal vector of the plane that bisects the angle between these two planes.  Then $\mathbf{n}$ is a unit vector in the direction of $\mathbf{n}_1 + \mathbf{n}_2,$ so
\[\mathbf{n} = \frac{\mathbf{n}_1 + \mathbf{n}_2}{||\mathbf{n}_1 + \mathbf{n}_2||} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{149}} \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -18 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}.\]Thus, the equation of the plane is of the form
\[7x - 18y + 5z + D = 0.\]Since this plane contains $(-5,-1,-5),$
\[7(-5) - 18(-1) + 5(-5) + D = 0,\]so $D = 22.$  Therefore, the equation of the plane is $\boxed{7x - 18y + 5z + 22 = 0}.$
TERMINATE

